the book of boba fett has finally come  to a close as the famous bounty hunter  rallies his forces for battle against  the pike syndicate and its enforcer cad  bain the series goes in some interesting  directions in chapter 5 and chapter 6  which heavily focus on the mandalorian  dinjarin the yoda lookalike grogu and  the legendary luke skywalker but the  finale brings everything back to  tatooine as boba's battle with the pikes  escalates into an all-out war across  moss espa does the finale have  ramifications for the wider star wars  universe more importantly does it tease  what's coming up ahead in the  mandalorian season 3 well sort of  for now  we wait the tension on tatooine cranks  up from the very beginning of the final  season one episode as boba finic shand  and the mandalorians survey the  sanctuary wreckage r.i.p guards with  whip boba also faces an emotional blow  as bane reveals that the pikes are  actually the ones who killed the tuscan  tribe not the nicto sand riders the  massacre is revenge for their attack on  the spice train all of this only hardens  boba's determination to rid tatooine of  the syndicate once and for all but when  the battle for masaspa gets started  writer john favreau and director robert  rodriguez deliver a pulse-pounding fight  for the very soul of tatooine luckily  boba dyn and finnick aren't alone in  their struggle the big cliffhanger at  the end of chapter 6 sees luke skywalker  offer grogu a choice he can either take  the best guard chain mail and return to  din jaren or he can pick yoda's old  lightsaber and train to become a  fully-fledged jedi on one hand it would  be great to see him train in the force  and master his abilities but we all know  that he really belongs with his  surrogate father thankfully favreau  gives fans what they want as r2d2 lands  luke's x-wing in pelimoto's hangar with  grogu sitting comfortably in the pilot  seat because grogu's memory is clouded  he doesn't have many meaningful  connections and although luke and ahsoka  tano are kind to him he's got a much  closer bond with den at least his brief  time with luke means he already has a  better grip on his force abilities than  he did before which is quite useful when  the streets of moss espa erupt into a  deadly fire fight when the other gangs  of the city betray their treaty with  boba attacking boba's enforcers it's not  exactly surprising since the different  factions are clearly just out for money  rather than respect although things  start to look dire when the hordes of  pykes deploy two deadly scorpenic droids  oh dear nevertheless boba has some other  backup to rely on  the devastating power of the scorpenec  droids causes chaos in the battle  because their shields are too strong for  boba's army to blast through with any of  their weapons dinjarin even whips out  the darksaber to try to penetrate the  shields but it has no effect at all  although he probably needs some more  training to carry its way but then the  finale pays off on chapter 3's promise  as boba finally rides his rancor into  battle the monster's power quickly  overwhelms the first scorpenec droid  with a little help from grogo luke's  training comes in handy for the little  green force user as he yanks a key  component from the droid's parts that  makes it vulnerable rogue clearly has a  fondness for shiny metal objects because  it's pretty reminiscent of the way he  grabs that ball from the razor crest in  the mandalorian season one after the  rancor finishes the first droid off boba  steers it to the second quickly  eviscerating it the destruction of the  droids and the sheer power of the rancor  sends the pikes running which is a nice  piece of symbolism tatooine is taking  itself back from its oppressors although  it's not over just yet as cad bane shows  his face again to try to kill boba kad  bane's arrival at the end of chapter 6  calls back to the western genre which  george lucas was originally inspired by  when creating star wars back in the 70s  director robert rodriguez leans into the  gun slinging genre once again for boba  fett's duel with bane in the finale as  they trade insults in a tense standoff  bane even points out they've known each  other a long time calling back to the  times they crossed paths during the  clone wars animated series bane makes it  clear that he might be an old man but  he's still quicker than bobo when it  comes to a quick draw gunfight for a  minute it even looks like bane might  kill boba look out for yourself  anything  is weakness  but this is boba fett so he doesn't go  down that easily instead he uses his  gaffy stick to swiftly knock bane to the  ground symbolizing how his new strength  comes from having a family he even  avenges his fallen tuscan tribe by  killing bane with the stick sure he's a  fan favorite villain but his death has  been a long time coming  cad bane's death causes the few  remaining pikes to retreat let's face it  if he can't take boba fett down who can  so it looks like this is a new era for  tatooine now that the crime lord has  liberated the planet from the pike  syndicate finnic shand even wipes out  that gang's last foothold on the planet  by killing their leader and executing  mayor mock shays leaving either of them  alive would mean that the spice trade on  tatooine could start up again sometime  after the big battle fett reacts  uncomfortably to the moss espa residents  bowing and calling him lord boba he  remarks to fennec that they're not cut  out to rule a surprising comment  considering everything they've gone  through to get here however this is a  new role for fett murderous bounty  hunter turned local hero fennec responds  if not us  then who the finale ends with den flying  his naboo starfighter through space as  grogu sits in the pod behind him the  little green force user even pesters him  to fly at high speeds and then like any  parent reluctantly obliges it's not  clear where they're headed although it's  possible den wants to redeem himself in  the waters of mandalore underneath the  planet's minds  of course it wouldn't be a disney plus  series if there wasn't a post-credits  scene teasing the future of the galaxy  the brief scene takes audiences back to  boba's quarters where cobb banff is  recuperating in the gunslinger's back to  tank where the modifier from chapter 4  is keeping an eye on him this clearly  suggests that van is severely wounded  when shot by cad bane but not killed  it'll be interesting to see how the  modification artist fixes his injuries  although he's definitely going to need  some new armor to wear instead of just a  shirt and a bandana maybe denjarin can  give him some spare besgar in the  mandalorian season 3.  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  the book of boba fett are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  you
 

